From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Atkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hwmontemp: add NCT6796 sensor type

The ASRock Rack X570D4I-2T carries a Nuvoton NCT6796D Super-I/O
hardware monitor, reachable from the BMC over its i2c back door at
1-002d. The stock AMI MegaRAC firmware drives it as an NCT6796D
(libipmipar.so exports dev_nct6796d_v0dot1_*).

Only NCT6779 was selectable, and nct6775_i2c_probe() takes the chip
kind straight from the i2c_device_id with no chip-ID verification, so
binding an NCT6796D as "nct6779" silently applies the wrong
temperature configuration: NCT6779_TEMP_MASK is 0x07ffff7e where
NCT6796_TEMP_MASK is 0xbfff0ffe, and the two temp_label tables diverge
from index 7 onward (nct6779 has "" / SMBUSMASTER 0-3 where nct6796
has AUXTIN4 / SMBUSMASTER 0-1 / Virtual_TEMP). The register maps are
shared, so temp1/SYSTIN happens to survive, but every source above it
is mislabelled or missing.

The kernel's nct6775-i2c driver already carries an "nct6796" entry in
nct6775_i2c_id, so this only needs plumbing through.

Signed-off-by: Nick Atkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
---
 src/hwmon-temp/HwmonTempMain.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/hwmon-temp/HwmonTempMain.cpp b/src/hwmon-temp/HwmonTempMain.cpp
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/src/hwmon-temp/HwmonTempMain.cpp
+++ b/src/hwmon-temp/HwmonTempMain.cpp
@@ -84,6 +84,7 @@ static constexpr auto sensorTypes =
         {"MAX6639", I2CDeviceType{"max6639", true}},
         {"MCP9600", I2CDeviceType{"mcp9600", false}},
         {"NCT6779", I2CDeviceType{"nct6779", true}},
+        {"NCT6796", I2CDeviceType{"nct6796", true}},
         {"NCT7802", I2CDeviceType{"nct7802", true}},
         {"PT5161L", I2CDeviceType{"pt5161l", true}},
         {"SBTSI", I2CDeviceType{"sbtsi", true}},
